data: {"messages":[{"content":"请判断哪些目标进入了指定区域、在区域内占用了多大空间，以及该区域是否出现超容量占用。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"d0d5752e-81ea-4e4e-8a12-770757e00e30"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_event_impact</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to evaluate the impact of an external event such as rainstorm, sports event, traffic control, holiday, emergency, or policy intervention on regional trajectory volume.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_event_impact/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_od_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks for OD flow analysis, origin-destination matrices, commute corridors, migration routes, or region-to-region movement aggregation from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_od_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_region_heat</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to compute regional activity heat, check-in volume, point density, unique users, or Top-K active geohash regions from trajectory records.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_region_heat/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to compute trajectory-based isochrones, reachable areas, travel-time accessibility, radiation range, or real mobility coverage from a starting geohash.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>anonymize_trajectory_data</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to anonymize, desensitize, privacy-protect, differentially perturb, k-anonymize, hash user IDs, grid-generalize, or prepare sensitive GPS/check-in trajectory data before retrieval or LLM analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/anonymize_trajectory_data/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>classify_trajectory_state</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to classify each user's trajectory into motion states such as stationary, directed migration, frequent circulation, random walk, cruising, long-stay, or semantic mobility behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/classify_trajectory_state/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>clean_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to clean raw GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or user mobility trajectory files by validating coordinates and timestamps, removing duplicates, filtering abnormal speed jumps, and exporting standardized cleaned trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/clean_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_flow_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect macro-level mobility flow anomalies, including abnormal region heat, check-in spikes, OD flow spikes, sudden decreases, or unusual time-window activity.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_flow_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_route_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect individual trip or route anomalies, such as unusually long distance, unusually long/short duration, abnormal average speed, detours, or trips that deviate from a user's usual behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_route_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_trajectory_cooccurrence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to detect co-occurrence, companion trajectories, contact tracing, crowd gathering, group convergence, or multiple users appearing in the same space-time window.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_trajectory_cooccurrence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>extract_stay_points</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to extract stay points, dwell events, OD endpoints, or meaningful stops from GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or cleaned trajectory data.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/extract_stay_points/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>forecast_region_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to predict future people or vehicle flow for target regions, based on historical regional activity series or raw trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/forecast_region_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>fuse_spatial_evidence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to combine hotspot, anomaly, profile, forecast, and event-impact outputs into a unified ranked regional evidence view.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/fuse_spatial_evidence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>map_spatial_grid</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to map latitude/longitude trajectory records, staypoints, trips, or check-ins into spatial grids such as Geohash for aggregation and downstream spatial analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/map_spatial_grid/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>measure_spatiotemporal_entropy</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to measure spatiotemporal entropy, mobility diversity, regional vitality, flow complexity, inflow-outflow variety, or urban activity index.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/measure_spatiotemporal_entropy/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>mine_trajectory_patterns</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to discover frequent travel patterns, recurring commuting sequences, repeated geohash chains, or multi-stop trip patterns from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/mine_trajectory_patterns/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>predict_next_location</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to predict next location, next stop, future geohash, likely destination, destination inference, or Markov-chain mobility prediction from historical trajectories.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/predict_next_location/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>profile_urban_region</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to identify urban functional regions such as residential, commercial, transit, leisure, or mixed-use areas by combining trajectory activity and POI evidence.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/profile_urban_region/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_similar_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to find historical trips or trajectory records similar to a target trip based on start/end position, travel distance, and duration.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_similar_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_spatiotemporal</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to search or recall trajectory records by time window, hour range, geohash prefix, bounding box, city, or semantic text condition.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_spatiotemporal/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"53e9cc35-2db8-4437-84f1-4a82d9f59a03"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：时空轨迹。场景ID：spatiotemporal_trajectory\n识别场景：时空轨迹 (spatiotemporal_trajectory)；场景模式：single；候选场景：spatiotemporal_trajectory\n任务切分：\n- 请判断哪些目标进入了指定区域、在区域内占用了多大空间，以及该区域是否出现超容量占用。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取时空轨迹数据与区域定义参数，解析目标对象的历史坐标序列，明确指定区域的几何边界及分析时间窗口，完成数据清洗与坐标系统一，输出结构化轨迹数据集与区域矢量范围。\n2. 基于时空轨迹场景的空间匹配能力，将目标对象的坐标序列与指定区域边界进行交集运算，筛选出实际进入该区域的目标清单，并记录其进入时间、离开时间及内部运动路径。\n3. 运用时空轨迹场景的轨迹聚合与空间测算能力，对进入区域的目标坐标点进行网格化或轮廓化处理，以轨迹覆盖面积占比或单位面积点密度作为关键指标，计算各目标及整体在区域内的空间占用量，产出量化占用数据。\n4. 依据预设的区域最大容纳标准或动态容量阈值作为判断口径，将步骤3产出的空间占用量与容量上限进行交叉比对，识别并标记超出阈值的时段或目标群体，产出超容量占用判定结论。\n5. 汇总上述分析结果，生成结构化交付文档，清晰列明进入目标列表、对应空间占用量化值、超容量判定结论及相关时空依据索引，确保分析过程可回溯。\n场景任务：\n- spatiotemporal_trajectory: 我将基于时空轨迹对指定区域进行分析，以判断进入该区域的目标、计算其空间占用量并判定是否出现超容量占用。；参数：{'分析对象': '目标', '空间范围': '指定区域', '分析目标': '空间占用与超容量分析'}\n已提取参数：{'分析对象': '目标', '空间范围': '指定区域', '分析目标': '空间占用与超容量分析'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：分析对象。轨迹主体，如人员、车辆、设备、事件、案件对象等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。需要分析的起止时间、日期、时段或相对时间\n- 提取可选参数：空间范围。轨迹涉及的区域、道路、地点、围栏或行政区划\n- 提取可选参数：分析目标。轨迹回放、停留点识别、路径分析、异常轨迹、同行分析、活动范围分析等\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"1b4daf88-ce12-461f-827f-ee607eb8d438"},{"content":"我需要先了解一些关键信息才能为您进行空间占用与超容量分析。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":716,"prompt_tokens":12659,"total_tokens":13375,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":399,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":716},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":12659}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-41727718-257e-9a9a-9a68-632f77c52525","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f73-f54b-7030-81ed-adad4e482857-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_clarification","args":{"context":"为了执行目标进入区域判断、空间占用量计算及超容量判定，需要您提供以下信息：\n1. **数据源**：是否有已上传的轨迹数据文件（如GPS记录、信令数据、签到数据等）？或者使用的是系统内置数据集？\n2. **分析对象**：目标是什么类型的人员、车辆、设备？是否需要指定特定ID或群体？\n3. **指定区域**：请提供区域的边界信息（如围栏坐标、Geohash前缀、行政区划名称、或具体地点名称）。\n4. **时间范围**：需要分析的起止时间或时段。\n5. **容量阈值**：该区域的最大容纳人数/数量标准是多少？还是由我根据某种规则自动推算？","question":"请提供以下参数以便进行分析：\n1. 轨迹数据来源（上传的文件或系统数据集名称）\n2. 分析的目标对象（人员/车辆/设备，或具体ID列表）\n3. 指定区域的定义方式（围栏坐标/Geohash/地名/行政区）\n4. 分析的时间窗口\n5. 区域容量上限标准（如有）","clarification_type":"missing_info","options":"[]"},"id":"call_0182926264dc49ac9c0846d1","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":12659,"output_tokens":716,"total_tokens":13375,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":399}}}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/0c5fb7bb-1371-4d88-a7db-8502379a36c6/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/0c5fb7bb-1371-4d88-a7db-8502379a36c6/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/0c5fb7bb-1371-4d88-a7db-8502379a36c6/user-data/outputs"},"artifacts":[],"raw_messages":[{"content":"请判断哪些目标进入了指定区域、在区域内占用了多大空间，以及该区域是否出现超容量占用。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"d0d5752e-81ea-4e4e-8a12-770757e00e30"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_event_impact</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to evaluate the impact of an external event such as rainstorm, sports event, traffic control, holiday, emergency, or policy intervention on regional trajectory volume.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_event_impact/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_od_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks for OD flow analysis, origin-destination matrices, commute corridors, migration routes, or region-to-region movement aggregation from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_od_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_region_heat</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to compute regional activity heat, check-in volume, point density, unique users, or Top-K active geohash regions from trajectory records.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_region_heat/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to compute trajectory-based isochrones, reachable areas, travel-time accessibility, radiation range, or real mobility coverage from a starting geohash.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>anonymize_trajectory_data</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to anonymize, desensitize, privacy-protect, differentially perturb, k-anonymize, hash user IDs, grid-generalize, or prepare sensitive GPS/check-in trajectory data before retrieval or LLM analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/anonymize_trajectory_data/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>classify_trajectory_state</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to classify each user's trajectory into motion states such as stationary, directed migration, frequent circulation, random walk, cruising, long-stay, or semantic mobility behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/classify_trajectory_state/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>clean_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to clean raw GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or user mobility trajectory files by validating coordinates and timestamps, removing duplicates, filtering abnormal speed jumps, and exporting standardized cleaned trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/clean_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_flow_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect macro-level mobility flow anomalies, including abnormal region heat, check-in spikes, OD flow spikes, sudden decreases, or unusual time-window activity.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_flow_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_route_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect individual trip or route anomalies, such as unusually long distance, unusually long/short duration, abnormal average speed, detours, or trips that deviate from a user's usual behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_route_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_trajectory_cooccurrence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to detect co-occurrence, companion trajectories, contact tracing, crowd gathering, group convergence, or multiple users appearing in the same space-time window.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_trajectory_cooccurrence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>extract_stay_points</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to extract stay points, dwell events, OD endpoints, or meaningful stops from GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or cleaned trajectory data.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/extract_stay_points/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>forecast_region_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to predict future people or vehicle flow for target regions, based on historical regional activity series or raw trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/forecast_region_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>fuse_spatial_evidence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to combine hotspot, anomaly, profile, forecast, and event-impact outputs into a unified ranked regional evidence view.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/fuse_spatial_evidence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>map_spatial_grid</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to map latitude/longitude trajectory records, staypoints, trips, or check-ins into spatial grids such as Geohash for aggregation and downstream spatial analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/map_spatial_grid/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>measure_spatiotemporal_entropy</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to measure spatiotemporal entropy, mobility diversity, regional vitality, flow complexity, inflow-outflow variety, or urban activity index.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/measure_spatiotemporal_entropy/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>mine_trajectory_patterns</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to discover frequent travel patterns, recurring commuting sequences, repeated geohash chains, or multi-stop trip patterns from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/mine_trajectory_patterns/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>predict_next_location</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to predict next location, next stop, future geohash, likely destination, destination inference, or Markov-chain mobility prediction from historical trajectories.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/predict_next_location/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>profile_urban_region</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to identify urban functional regions such as residential, commercial, transit, leisure, or mixed-use areas by combining trajectory activity and POI evidence.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/profile_urban_region/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_similar_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to find historical trips or trajectory records similar to a target trip based on start/end position, travel distance, and duration.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_similar_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_spatiotemporal</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to search or recall trajectory records by time window, hour range, geohash prefix, bounding box, city, or semantic text condition.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_spatiotemporal/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"53e9cc35-2db8-4437-84f1-4a82d9f59a03"}],"viewed_images":{},"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请判断哪些目标进入了指定区域、在区域内占用了多大空间，以及该区域是否出现超容量占用。","normalized_query":"请判断哪些目标进入了指定区域、在区域内占用了多大空间，以及该区域是否出现超容量占用。","routing_query":"场景：时空轨迹。场景ID：spatiotemporal_trajectory。场景说明：人员、车辆、设备、事件等对象的时间序列位置、轨迹回放、停留点、路径、活动范围和时空关联分析场景。需要识别参数：分析对象、时间范围、空间范围、分析目标。用户原始问题：我将基于时空轨迹对指定区域进行分析，以判断进入该区域的目标、计算其空间占用量并判定是否出现超容量占用","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","params":{"分析对象":"目标","空间范围":"指定区域","分析目标":"空间占用与超容量分析"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["spatiotemporal_trajectory"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_e7092b","text":"请判断哪些目标进入了指定区域、在区域内占用了多大空间，以及该区域是否出现超容量占用。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_520466","text":"读取时空轨迹数据与区域定义参数，解析目标对象的历史坐标序列，明确指定区域的几何边界及分析时间窗口，完成数据清洗与坐标系统一，输出结构化轨迹数据集与区域矢量范围。"},{"task_span_id":"span_f9bf4e","text":"基于时空轨迹场景的空间匹配能力，将目标对象的坐标序列与指定区域边界进行交集运算，筛选出实际进入该区域的目标清单，并记录其进入时间、离开时间及内部运动路径。"},{"task_span_id":"span_a10493","text":"运用时空轨迹场景的轨迹聚合与空间测算能力，对进入区域的目标坐标点进行网格化或轮廓化处理，以轨迹覆盖面积占比或单位面积点密度作为关键指标，计算各目标及整体在区域内的空间占用量，产出量化占用数据。"},{"task_span_id":"span_604da7","text":"依据预设的区域最大容纳标准或动态容量阈值作为判断口径，将步骤3产出的空间占用量与容量上限进行交叉比对，识别并标记超出阈值的时段或目标群体，产出超容量占用判定结论。"},{"task_span_id":"span_2f6d66","text":"汇总上述分析结果，生成结构化交付文档，清晰列明进入目标列表、对应空间占用量化值、超容量判定结论及相关时空依据索引，确保分析过程可回溯。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_ab74ce","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","text":"我将基于时空轨迹对指定区域进行分析，以判断进入该区域的目标、计算其空间占用量并判定是否出现超容量占用。","params":{"分析对象":"目标","空间范围":"指定区域","分析目标":"空间占用与超容量分析"}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_ab74ce","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","text":"我将基于时空轨迹对指定区域进行分析，以判断进入该区域的目标、计算其空间占用量并判定是否出现超容量占用。","params":{"分析对象":"目标","空间范围":"指定区域","分析目标":"空间占用与超容量分析"}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：分析对象。轨迹主体，如人员、车辆、设备、事件、案件对象等","提取可选参数：时间范围。需要分析的起止时间、日期、时段或相对时间","提取可选参数：空间范围。轨迹涉及的区域、道路、地点、围栏或行政区划","提取可选参数：分析目标。轨迹回放、停留点识别、路径分析、异常轨迹、同行分析、活动范围分析等"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:d0d5752e-81ea-4e4e-8a12-770757e00e30"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":true,"primary_goal":"请判断哪些目标进入了指定区域、在区域内占用了多大空间，以及该区域是否出现超容量占用。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请判断哪些目标进入了指定区域、在区域内占用了多大空间，以及该区域是否出现超容量占用。","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[{"id":"analyze_event_impact","role":"primary","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_od_flow","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_region_heat","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"anonymize_trajectory_data","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"classify_trajectory_state","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"clean_trajectory","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"detect_flow_anomaly","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"detect_route_anomaly","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"detect_trajectory_cooccurrence","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"extract_stay_points","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"forecast_region_flow","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"fuse_spatial_evidence","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"map_spatial_grid","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"measure_spatiotemporal_entropy","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"mine_trajectory_patterns","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"predict_next_location","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"profile_urban_region","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"search_similar_trajectory","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"search_spatiotemporal","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null}],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":["analyze_event_impact","analyze_od_flow","analyze_region_heat","analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","anonymize_trajectory_data","classify_trajectory_state","clean_trajectory","detect_flow_anomaly","detect_route_anomaly","detect_trajectory_cooccurrence","extract_stay_points","forecast_region_flow","fuse_spatial_evidence","map_spatial_grid","measure_spatiotemporal_entropy","mine_trajectory_patterns","predict_next_location","profile_urban_region","search_similar_trajectory","search_spatiotemporal"],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":1.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":["analyze_event_impact","analyze_od_flow","analyze_region_heat","analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","anonymize_trajectory_data","classify_trajectory_state","clean_trajectory","detect_flow_anomaly","detect_route_anomaly","detect_trajectory_cooccurrence","extract_stay_points","forecast_region_flow","fuse_spatial_evidence","map_spatial_grid","measure_spatiotemporal_entropy","mine_trajectory_patterns","predict_next_location","profile_urban_region","search_similar_trajectory","search_spatiotemporal"],"selection_owner":"lead_agent","_source_message_key":"id:d0d5752e-81ea-4e4e-8a12-770757e00e30"},"dialogue_context":{"act":"new_task","confidence":0.7,"reason":"no_pending_action_match","parsed_answer":null,"pending_action_id":null,"resume_intent_context":null,"resume_routing_context":null,"metadata":{}},"final_scope_skill_ids":["analyze_event_impact","analyze_od_flow","analyze_region_heat","analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","anonymize_trajectory_data","classify_trajectory_state","clean_trajectory","detect_flow_anomaly","detect_route_anomaly","detect_trajectory_cooccurrence","extract_stay_points","forecast_region_flow","fuse_spatial_evidence","map_spatial_grid","measure_spatiotemporal_entropy","mine_trajectory_patterns","predict_next_location","profile_urban_region","search_similar_trajectory","search_spatiotemporal"],"allowed_tool_names":[]}

